**How to implement.** The product check, the combined QZ+LR matrix against the cascade M_LR · M_QZ, becomes part of the staged path's answer, with the product-check RMSE ratio the reference reports (001 §L 'the product check for series objects (M_comb against M_LR · M_QZ)'; 001 §Q AT-1 'Assertions: … the product-check RMSE ratio'; the S10.3 brief 'the cascade comparison' and 'It returns … the product check'; S11.4 reuses it). The reference computes `fit_rmse`, the combined matrix's own RMSE over its rows, and `product_rmse`, the cascade's prediction RMSE over the same rows (`Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/matrix_fit_linear.py:372-373`, in `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/` from step 329), and its report prints `product / fit` (`:334`). (0) The residual RMSE of a solution over a least-squares system gets one implementation, which the SVD proxy and the product check share (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy … A duplicated function body … is a defect'): `createMathNetSvd` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:createMathNetSvd`) computes `‖A·x − b‖ / √m` inline today, in its `residual`, `rows` and `rmse` bindings. In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs` the record `LeastSquaresSystem` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:LeastSquaresSystem`) gains `member this.residualRmseAt (solution : RealVector) : ResidualRmse`: `RealMatrix.create` of its design rows' values times `solution`, minus `RealVector.create` of `rhs`, the difference's `norm` divided by `sqrt` of the row count, the expression `createMathNetSvd` evaluates, in its order (`ResidualRmse` is declared above the record, `MuellerReconstruction.fs:ResidualRmse`). Its doc, one to three lines: the residual RMSE of a solution over this system's rows, the one the solver reports and the product check reuses (spec 0050 S10.3). In `createMathNetSvd` those three bindings become `system.residualRmseAt (RealVector x)`; its checks, its errors and the rest of its body are unchanged, so every solver RMSE is the same double, as `the real createMathNetSvd proxy solves a known over-determined full-rank system`, `reconstruct recovers a seeded MuellerMatrix from a synthetic full-rank design at rank 16 (always-run)`, `freeCosineFit recovers a synthetic cosine zero and visibility within tolerance (always-run)` and the section 7.2 fact, which read it through the proxy, show. No other declaration of the file changes. (1) In `StagedMuellerPath.fs`, before `StagedMuellerData`: (a) `ProductRmseRatio of float` with `member this.value`, doc one line, and `static member between (productRmse : ResidualRmse) (fitRmse : ResidualRmse) : ProductRmseRatio` (`productRmse.value / fitRmse.value`), the one place the ratio is formed, as `RelativeError.between` is (step 338). (b) `ProductCheckData = { cascade : MuellerMatrix; difference : MatrixDiff; fitRmse : ResidualRmse; productRmse : ResidualRmse }` with `member this.rmseRatio : ProductRmseRatio` (`ProductRmseRatio.between this.productRmse this.fitRmse`). (c) `productCheckOf (lr : MuellerMatrix) (qz : MuellerMatrix) (combined : ReconstructedMatrix) (combinedSystem : LeastSquaresSystem) : ProductCheckData`: `cascade` is `cascadeProduct lr qz` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:cascadeProduct`, in its operand order), `difference` is `frobeniusDiff combined.matrix cascade` (`:frobeniusDiff`), `fitRmse` is `combined.rmse` and `productRmse` is `combinedSystem.residualRmseAt cascade.vecColumnMajor` (part 0). (2) `StagedMuellerData` gains `productCheck : ProductCheckData` after `qzLr`; `reconstructStaged` keeps the `QzLrProduct` system it solves and fills the field with `productCheckOf lr.matrix qz.matrix qzLr` of that system, after the three solves. (3) `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/MuellerReference.fs` opens `OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath` and gains, after the gains, `combinedFitRmse` = `ResidualRmse 0.10162659513724465` (`combined_check.fit_rmse`), `productRmse` = `ResidualRmse 0.12833930975940816` (`combined_check.product_rmse`) and `productCheckRmseRatio` = `ProductRmseRatio.between productRmse combinedFitRmse`. `dataMatrixTol`'s doc gains one line: it also bands the ratio, whose observed deviation was 5.7e-13 when spec 0050 was authored, 2026-11-04. (4) `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs`: the section 7.2 fact's cascade check reads `staged.productCheck` and its own `cascadeProduct` and `frobeniusDiff` calls go: the three metrics are `staged.productCheck.difference`'s, compared with `MuellerReference`'s at `MuellerReference.dataMatrixTol` as before, and the two largest-delta positions compare `staged.qzLr.matrix` with `staged.productCheck.cascade`. It gains one assertion: `staged.productCheck.rmseRatio` is within `MuellerReference.dataMatrixTol` of `MuellerReference.productCheckRmseRatio`, its message naming the two RMSEs and the two ratios. (5) Test, in `StagedMuellerPathTests`: `the product check compares the combined matrix with the cascade and the RMSEs over the combined rows`: with `lr` = `Propagation.identityMueller`, `qz` = the diagonal Mueller matrix diag(1, 0.5, 0.5, 1), `combined` = `{ matrix = Propagation.identityMueller; rank = MatrixRank 16; rmse = ResidualRmse 0.1 }` and the system of the two design rows `kron4 (StokesVector.create [ 1.0; 0.0; 0.0; 0.0 ]) (RealVector4.create [ 1.0; 0.0; 0.0; 0.0 ])` and the same two constructors over [ 0.0; 1.0; 0.0; 0.0 ] (they read M₀₀ and M₁₁, `MuellerReconstruction.fs:kron4`) with the right-hand side 1.0 and 0.8, `productCheckOf` answers a `cascade` equal to `qz` element by element, a `difference` whose `maxAbs` is 0.5 and whose `frobenius` is √0.5, `fitRmse` 0.1, `productRmse` √0.045 and a `rmseRatio` of √0.045 / 0.1, each within 1e-12. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'; 001 §S10 '`BerremanTests` stays green with unchanged numbers'): the three metrics and the two positions are computed from the same matrices by the same calls, and every solver RMSE by the same operations. A probe this spec ran at authoring reproduced the summary's `fit_rmse`, `product_rmse` and their ratio within 2.3e-14, 2.9e-14 and 5.7e-13, so the new assertion holds at `dataMatrixTol`. `MuellerReconstructionTests`' count is unchanged.

**Acceptance.** After the product check lands, `LeastSquaresSystem.residualRmseAt` MUST compute `‖A·x − b‖ / √m` and `createMathNetSvd` MUST report its RMSE through it, `productCheckOf` MUST answer the cascade M_LR · M_QZ, its difference from M_{QZ+LR}, the combined fit's RMSE and the cascade's RMSE over the combined rows, and their ratio, `reconstructStaged` MUST carry it, and the section 7.2 fact MUST read it, finding the ratio within `MuellerReference.dataMatrixTol` of `MuellerReference.productCheckRmseRatio`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the product check compares the combined matrix with the cascade and the RMSEs over the combined rows`, the count rising by 1; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s35 invariants MUST pass.
